"// resolveHost is musl's name lookup: a numeric host, else the lines of /etc/hosts naming it, each address once,"] [287 1 "// sorted by precedence; canon the first line's canonical name (the literal for a numeric host)."] [291 24 "// AI_V4MAPPED"] [306 4 "// inet_aton's forms: 127.1, 0x7f.1, a single number"] [312 22 "// AI_NUMERICHOST"] [345 1 "// inetAton is inet_aton(3): a.b.c.d, a.b.c, a.b or a, each part decimal, octal or hex."] [397 1 "// sockaddrArg is getsockaddrarg: an address object of the socket's family as a syscall.Sockaddr."] [429 23 "// a file named \"@...\": Go's SockaddrUnix reads a leading '@' as the abstract namespace"] [509 1 "// sockaddrObj is makesockaddr: a syscall.Sockaddr as CPython's address object."] [518 22 "// unnamed (Go's anyToSockaddr turns its empty path's NUL into '@')"] [537 1 "// ---- buffers"] [539 1 "// writableBuf is a writable bytes-like object's bytes: a bytearray, or a memoryview of one."] [781 25 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [1595 21 "// NI_NUMERICHOST"] [1598 29 "// NI_NAMEREQD"] [1603 21 "// NI_NUMERICSERV"] [1605 23 "// NI_DGRAM"] [1788 4 "// CPython's get_CMSG_LEN and get_CMSG_SPACE: the length at most socklen_t's limit less CMSG_LEN(0),"] [1789 4 "// or less CMSG_SPACE(1)"] [1805 1 "// hostsName is /etc/hosts' canonical name of an address, \"\" when none."] [1873 1 "// getaddrinfo is musl's: the host's addresses (numeric, /etc/hosts; None: loopback, or any with AI_PASSIVE) times"] [1874 1 "// the socket types asked (0: stream and datagram), canonname always set as musl sets it."] [1882 32 "// AI_NUMERICSERV"] [1907 21 "// AI_PASSIVE"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[43 34] [156 46] [259 39] [289 36] [301 36] [305 29] [307 30] [367 12] [367 21] [377 12] [377 21] [412 53] [490 36] [498 44] [500 42] [548 34] [556 24] [563 24] [690 31] [701 48] [712 49] [731 42] [738 36] [755 43] [802 36] [810 45] [826 48] [845 42] [868 45] [904 36] [945 42] [964 46] [